538-I demonstrate the use of the new formulae on an \textit{RXTE} observation of Cygnus X-1 in the hard state (obsid 10238-01-06-00). This observation has been used for a number of spectral-timing studies (e.g. \citealt{Gilfanov2000,Mastroserio2018,Mahmoud2018}). Most significantly for the purposes of this paper, \cite{Mastroserio2019} fit the X-ray reverberation model \textsc{reltrans} \citep{Ingram2019} to the real and imaginary parts of the energy-dependent cross-spectrum for 10 frequency ranges (plus the time-average spectrum) in order to yield a black hole mass measurement, but the best fitting model had a reduced $\chi^2$ of $0.76$. It turns out that this over-fitting occurred because the error bars were calculated in the single cross-spectrum limit relevant to the \cite{Bendat2010} formulae, when the error formulae derived in this paper would instead have been appropriate.
