675-
676-{It seems possible}
677-% The reader may worry
678-that the use of incorrect error formulae in the literature has led to many erroneous results. This is not the case though - the conclusions of previous studies are unlikely to be significantly changed by adoption of the new error formulae (see e.g. Section \ref{sec:data}), {since the new formulae are in the most part subtle corrections to the old formulae.}
679-% This is unsurprising on reflection, since there is nothing more obvious than error bars that are far too large, and so the over-fitting that has made it into the literature has been necessarily subtle.
